---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import ArticleImage from "../../components/ui/ArticleImage.astro";
import Sources from "../../components/ui/Sources.astro";
import type { FaqItem } from "../../lib/seo";

const faqs: FaqItem[] = [
  { q: "How do I count alcohol calories?", a: "Treat alcohol calories like any other calorie. Our <a href='/alcohol-calories-calculator/'>alcohol calories calculator</a> estimates calories from beer, wine, and spirits." },
  { q: "Does alcohol affect weight loss?", a: "Yes. Alcohol supplies 7 kcal/g and pauses fat burning while the liver metabolizes ethanol." },
  { q: "Which drinks are lowest in calories?", a: "Straight spirits with zero-calorie mixers are lowest, followed by dry wine and light beer." },
  { q: "Can I drink alcohol on a diet?", a: "Yes, if you account for the calories and fit them within your daily target." },
  { q: "How many calories in a standard drink?", a: "A standard drink contains about 14 g of alcohol, roughly 98 calories from alcohol alone." },
  { q: "Do mixers add calories?", a: "Yes. Regular soda, juice, and syrups can add 100-200 calories per mixed drink." },
  { q: "Does alcohol stop fat burning?", a: "The liver prioritizes metabolizing ethanol before oxidizing fat, so fat burning slows temporarily." },
];

---

<ContentLayout
  title="Alcohol Calorie Counter — Complete Guide to Alcohol Calories"
  h1="Alcohol Calorie Counter"
  description="Count calories in beer, wine, spirits, and mixed drinks. Learn how alcohol calories work and get tips for drinking on a diet."
  path="/guides/alcohol-calorie-counter/"
  category="Guides"
  categoryPath="/guides/"
  lead="Alcohol has 7 calories per gram and pauses fat burning. Here is how to count calories in your favorite drinks."
  updated="July 2026"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p>An <strong>alcohol calorie counter</strong> estimates calories in beer, wine, spirits, and mixed drinks. Alcohol contains 7 kcal per gram, more than carbs or protein (4 kcal/g) but less than fat (9 kcal/g).</p>

  <ArticleImage src="/assets/images/articles/alcohol-calories.svg" alt="Illustration of various alcoholic beverages with calorie counter overlay." />

  <h2>How to count alcohol calories</h2>
  <p>Use the formula: ethanol ml = volume x (ABV / 100), then ethanol grams = ethanol ml x 0.789, then alcohol calories = ethanol grams x 7. Our <a href="/alcohol-calories-calculator/">alcohol calories calculator</a> does this automatically.</p>

  <h2>Common beverages calorie table</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Drink</th><th>Serving</th><th>ABV</th><th>Calories</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Light beer</td><td>12 oz</td><td>~4%</td><td>~90-120 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Regular beer</td><td>12 oz</td><td>~5%</td><td>~140-160 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Craft IPA</td><td>12 oz</td><td>~7%</td><td>~200-250 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Red wine</td><td>5 oz</td><td>~12%</td><td>~100-125 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>White wine</td><td>5 oz</td><td>~11%</td><td>~90-110 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Dessert wine</td><td>3.5 oz</td><td>~18%</td><td>~140-160 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Vodka shot</td><td>1.5 oz</td><td>40%</td><td>~100 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Whiskey shot</td><td>1.5 oz</td><td>40%</td><td>~100 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Margarita</td><td>12 oz</td><td>~12%</td><td>~300-400 kcal</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pina colada</td><td>12 oz</td><td>~15%</td><td>~300-500 kcal</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>How alcohol affects metabolism and fat loss</h2>
  <p>Alcohol metabolism takes priority over fat oxidation in the liver. While alcohol is being cleared, fat burning slows temporarily. Alcohol also impairs recovery, raises cortisol, and can increase hunger.</p>

  <h2>Strategies for moderate drinking on a diet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Budget alcohol calories ahead by reducing carbs or fat elsewhere.</li>
    <li>Choose lower-ABV options and avoid sugary mixers.</li>
    <li>Log alcohol in your food diary just like any other food.</li>
    <li>Drink water between alcoholic drinks to slow intake.</li>
    <li>Pair alcohol with a high-protein meal to help control appetite.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Related calculators</h2>
  <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="card p-4">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink"><a href="/alcohol-calories-calculator/">Alcohol Calories Calculator</a></h3>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-body">Get the exact calories in your drink by entering ABV and volume.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card p-4">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink"><a href="/macro-calculator/">Macro Calculator</a></h3>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-body">Adjust your daily macros to fit alcohol calories without derailing your diet.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Sources sources={[
    { label: "NIH - Alcohol Alert: Alcohol Metabolism", href: "https://www.niaaa.nih.gov/publications/alcohol-alerts/alcohol-metabolism" },
    { label: "Atwater system - Energy values of food components", href: "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3664764/" },
  ]} />
</ContentLayout>
